            0.347,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.086,
            0.463,
            0.109
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ Is a rectangle a parallelogram?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.111,
            0.849,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": "A rectangle has opposite sides parallel. So, it satisfies the parallelogram’s definition. Hence, it is indeed a parallelogram. More specifically, a rectangle is a special kind of parallelogram with all its angles equal to 90°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.185,
            0.682,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": "Let us represent this relation using a Venn diagram."
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.215,
            0.732,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_chart_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.431,
            0.848,
            0.471
          ],
          "content": "To understand the relations between the sides and the angles of a parallelogram, let us construct the following figure."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.507,
            0.515,
            0.566
          ],
          "content": "？ Draw a parallelogram with adjacent sides of lengths 4 cm and 5 cm, and an angle of 30° between them."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.571,
            0.378,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.627,
            0.516,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": "**Step 1:** Draw line segments AB = 4 cm and AD = 5 cm with an angle of 30° between them."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.516,
            0.473,
            0.939,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.717,
            0.515,
            0.812
          ],
          "content": "**Step 2:** Draw a line parallel to AB through the point D, and a line parallel to AD through B. Mark the point at which these lines intersect as C."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.818,
            0.514,
            0.84
          ],
          "content": "ABCD is the required parallelogram."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.548,
            0.712,
            0.923,
            0.831
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.853,
            0.849,
            0.912
          ],
          "content": "？ What are the remaining angles of the parallelogram? What are the lengths of the remaining sides? See if you can reason out and/or experiment to figure these out."
        },
        {
